Why: NewDockerClient calls GET /info first and log.Fatal's the whole server when it
fails (backend/pkg/docker/client.go:139-142, cmd/pentagi/main.go:221-224). The cell's
cell-guard deliberately refuses /info (it describes the host daemon). PentAGI only
uses the answer for a startup log line and for the sandbox probe's daemon id, which
runs only with DOCKER_INSIDE=true (off here), so a refused /info is now a warning.
Touches backend/pkg/docker/client.go.

